# L0 / B008 — ef-core, git-workflow, health-check, http-api, httpclient-factory (+resilience).

C R203 OL GOV-015 | MUST NOT | Do not commit, push, merge, rebase, reset, force-push, delete or rename branches or perform other repository-changing Git operations unless explicitly requested; never force-push a shared branch unless the user explicitly requests history rewriting. | Git operations | Explicit request.
C R204 OL GOV-016 | MUST | Parallel implementation streams use separate branches and worktrees (one branch is not checked out in several normal worktrees); keep unrelated changes out of the current branch. | parallel work | none stated
C R205 OL GOV-019 | MUST NOT | Never discard, overwrite, reset, clean or otherwise destroy user work to make a Git operation easier; never remove a worktree containing uncommitted user work; do not automatically stash, reset or discard local work for a merge or rebase. | Git operations | none stated
C R206 OL GOV-020 | MUST | Before any repository-changing operation inspect the relevant state (status, diffs, what a high-risk operation would lose or rewrite) and use the minimum operation required; do not silently clean up unrelated working-tree changes. | Git operations | none stated
C R207 OL WF-022 | MUST | Before committing inspect the staged diff and include only the requested logical change; do not stage unrelated modified files; one logical change per commit with its tests, no artificial tiny commits or combined unrelated fixes; before pushing confirm branch and state, ensure relevant verification completed and avoid pushing unrelated local commits. | commits and pushes | none stated
C U2 LU GOV-015 | MUST NOT (conditional) | git reset --hard, git clean, git push --force / --force-with-lease, branch deletion and rebasing shared history are performed only when explicitly requested or clearly required by an approved workflow, after inspecting what will be lost or rewritten. | high-risk Git operations | 'clearly required by an approved workflow' | GOV-015 permits repository-changing Git operations only on explicit request; 'clearly required by an approved workflow' names no workflow and may authorize high-risk operations without an explicit request, or may only refer to an explicitly approved procedure. | Under the broad reading an agent could force-push or delete a branch because a workflow requires it, without an explicit request.
C X18 EX GOV-015,GOV-019 | MUST NOT | Treat main, master and other protected/shared branches as non-rewritable. | Git history rewriting | none stated | GOV-015 allows repository-changing operations, including history rewriting, on explicit request; this rule forbids rewriting these branches without an approval path. | Even when the user explicitly asks to force-push a rewritten main, the instruction tells the agent not to rewrite it.
C X19 EX WF-009 | MUST | A pull request has a focused purpose and its description explains what changed, why, how it was verified, and compatibility/migration notes. | pull request preparation | none stated | No oracle policy prescribes PR description contents; WF-009 only requires truthful verification reporting. | A PR description without the verification and migration notes does not follow the workflow.
C X20 EX RUN-002,ARC-017 | MUST NOT | Do not make fire-and-forget EF Core async calls (named anti-pattern). | EF Core usage | none stated | RUN-002 concerns blocking on async I/O and ARC-017 the shared scoped context; no oracle policy names unawaited (fire-and-forget) EF calls, which is EF technique turned into a prohibition. | Starting an EF Core SaveChangesAsync or query without awaiting it violates the instruction.
C X21 EX RUN-016,DEP-020 | MUST NOT | Do not wrap normal EF Core operations in a generic application-level retry pipeline; prefer the provider's EF Core execution strategy (e.g. EnableRetryOnFailure for SQL Server) and follow provider guidance for transaction/retry interaction. | database access resilience | none stated | RUN-016 governs when retries are safe and the oracle treats database-retry examples as conditional technique (EXC-007); no oracle policy forbids an application-level retry pipeline around EF Core operations. | Wrapping repository calls in a generic resilience retry pipeline violates the instruction even for idempotent reads.
C X22 EX RUN-005 | MUST NOT | Never mutate a shared HttpClient's DefaultRequestHeaders concurrently; apply per-request values such as dynamic tokens per request or through a handler. | outbound HTTP clients | none stated | RUN-005 governs client lifetime only; thread-safe header handling is client technique not stated by any oracle policy. | Setting a per-user token on DefaultRequestHeaders of a shared typed client per call violates the instruction.

